  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "On November 1, 2026, a privately owned Learjet 60 business jet crashed in Palm Beach County, Florida, United States.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383802284:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "John I. Leonard Community High School, near the crash site, was closed on November 2 while emergency crews and investigators continued operations nearby.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383802284:28"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "At a second press briefing on November 3, Chapman confirmed that the elevator had separated before impact.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383802284:41"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The aircraft set out from Austin–Bergstrom International Airport, bound for North Eleuthera Airport.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383802284:origin",
        "wiki:box:1383802284:destination"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:32Z",
      "text": "It came down about 1,760 km from Austin–Bergstrom International Airport in a straight line, with about 370 km still to go.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383802284:origin",
        "wiki:box:1383802284:destination",
        "wiki:box:1383802284:coordinates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:40Z",
      "text": "The aircraft crashed en route in Palm Beach County, and the summary records an in-flight structural failure, with the investigation still under way.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383802284:summary",
        "wiki:box:1383802284:coordinates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:49Z",
      "text": "The aircraft was a Learjet 60, built by Bombardier Aerospace, and the type first flew in 1990.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383802284:aircraft",
        "wd:Q1267393:P176",
        "wd:Q1267393:P606"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:53Z",
      "text": "It was operated by Aurora Aviation, doing business as Upper Jets.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383802284:operator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:58Z",
      "text": "All 9 people on board died: 7 passengers and 2 crew, according to the article.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383802284:occupants",
        "wiki:box:1383802284:fatalities",
        "wiki:box:1383802284:passengers",
        "wiki:box:1383802284:crew",
        "wiki:box:1383802284:survivors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:06Z",
      "text": "On the ground, according to the article, 1 person was injured.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383802284:ground-injuries"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:15Z",
      "text": "The aircraft departed Austin–Bergstrom International Airport at 10:37 EST (15:37 UTC).",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:timeline:1383802284:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:22Z",
      "text": "At 12:48 EST (17:48 UTC), the first officer radioed a mayday call to ATC, reporting a deteriorating situation.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:timeline:1383802284:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:31Z",
      "text": "The Palm Beach County Sheriff's Office closed Military Trail near the impact site to support the emergency response and investigation.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:investigation:1383802284:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:38Z",
      "text": "Thunderstorms were affecting the Palm Beach area around the time of the crash, with visibility of 2 to 10 mi and surface wind gusts of 20 to 30 mph.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:investigation:1383802284:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:45Z",
      "text": "According to recorded air traffic control communications, the crew reported light clear icing and moderate turbulence at approximately 35,000 ft, with altitude fluctuations of up to 700 ft.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:investigation:1383802284:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:53Z",
      "text": "Readers also turned to the Learjet 60 article, with 121,648 readers on 3 November 2026.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Learjet_60:2026-11-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:02:02Z",
      "text": "The article drew 132,447 readers on 3 November 2026, and it had no readers in the 8 to 60 days before, as a new article.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_Palm_Beach_County_Learjet_60_crash:2026-11-03",
        "views:en:2026_Palm_Beach_County_Learjet_60_crash:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:02:08Z",
      "text": "The article is read in 10 languages, and after English, the most readers are in German, with 9,654.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_Palm_Beach_County_Learjet_60_crash:2026-11-03",
        "views:de:Flugzeugabsturz_am_1._November_2026_in_Palm_Beach:2026-11-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:02:14Z",
      "text": "On the globe, each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers; a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
